msgstr ""
"# Quick Start Guide\n"
"\n"
"This guide will help you quickly get started with this project. Please follow the steps below to install, configure, and run the project.\n"
"\n"
"## Prerequisites\n"
"\n"
"Before starting, make sure your development environment meets the following requirements:\n"
"\n"
"- **Operating System**: Windows 10/11, macOS 10.15+, or Linux (Ubuntu 20.04+ recommended)\n"
"- **Node.js**: version 18.0 or higher\n"
"- **Package Manager**: npm 9.0+ or yarn 1.22+\n"
"- **Database**: MySQL 8.0+ or PostgreSQL 14+\n"
"\n"
"## Installation Steps\n"
"\n"
"### 1. Clone the Repository\n"
"\n"
"Open a terminal and run the following command to clone the project to your local machine:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"git clone https://github.com/your-username/your-project.git\n"
"cd your-project\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 2. Install Dependencies\n"
"\n"
"Use npm or yarn to install the project dependencies:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"# Using npm\n"
"npm install\n"
"\n"
"# Or using yarn\n"
"yarn install\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 3. Configure Environment Variables\n"
"\n"
"Create a `.env` file in the project root directory and copy the contents of the `.env.example` file into it. Then modify the configuration items according to your actual environment:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"cp .env.example .env\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Key configuration items:\n"
"\n"
"- `PORT`: Server port number, default is 3000\n"
"- `DB_HOST`: Database host address\n"
"- `DB_PORT`: Database port number\n"
"- `DB_USER`: Database username\n"
"- `DB_PASSWORD`: Database password\n"
"- `DB_NAME`: Database name\n"
"- `JWT_SECRET`: JWT encryption key, please use a sufficiently complex random string\n"
"\n"
"### 4. Initialize the Database\n"
"\n"
"Run the database migration command to create the required data tables:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"npm run migrate\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"If you need to populate test data, run:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"npm run seed\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### 5. Start the Development Server\n"
"\n"
"Run the following command to start the development server:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"After successful startup, you will see output similar to the following:\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"Server running at http://localhost:3000\n"
"Database connection established successfully\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Project Structure\n"
"\n"
"Here is the basic directory structure of the project:\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"your-project/\n"
"├── src/                  # Source code directory\n"
"│   ├── controllers/      # Controllers\n"
"│   ├── models/           # Data models\n"
"│   ├── routes/           # Route definitions\n"
"│   ├── services/         # Business logic layer\n"
"│   ├── middlewares/      # Middleware\n"
"│   ├── utils/            # Utility functions\n"
"│   └── app.js            # Application entry file\n"
"├── config/               # Configuration files\n"
"├── tests/                # Test files\n"
"├── public/               # Static resources\n"
"├── .env.example          # Environment variable example file\n"
"├── package.json          # Project dependency and script configuration\n"
"└── README.md             # Project documentation\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Common Commands\n"
"\n"
"- `npm run dev`: Start the development server (with hot reload)\n"
"- `npm run build`: Build the production version\n"
"- `npm start`: Start the production server\n"
"- `npm test`: Run the test suite\n"
"- `npm run lint`: Run code style checking\n"
"- `npm run format`: Automatically format code\n"
"\n"
"## API Documentation\n"
"\n"
"After starting the project, you can view the automatically generated API documentation by visiting the following address:\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"http://localhost:3000/api-docs\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Troubleshooting\n"
"\n"
"### Port Occupied\n"
"\n"
"If port 3000 is already occupied, you can modify the `PORT` configuration in the `.env` file, or use the following command to find and terminate the process occupying the port:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"# Linux/macOS\n"
"lsof -i :3000\n"
"\n"
"# Windows\n"
"netstat -ano | findstr :3000\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### Database Connection Failure\n"
"\n"
"Please check:\n"
"\n"
"1. Whether the database service has been started\n"
"2. Whether the database connection information in the `.env` file is correct\n"
"3. Whether the database user has sufficient permissions\n"
"\n"
"### Dependency Installation Failure\n"
"\n"
"Try clearing the cache and reinstalling:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"npm cache clean --force\n"
"rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json\n"
"npm install\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Next Steps\n"
"\n"
"- Read the [Configuration Guide](./configuration.md) to learn about more configuration options\n"
"- Read the [API Reference](./api-reference.md) to understand all available interfaces\n"
"- Read the [Deployment Guide](./deployment.md) to learn how to deploy to a production environment\n"
"\n"
"## Getting Help\n"
"\n"
"If you encounter any problems, you can:\n"
"\n"
"- Submit an issue on [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/your-username/your-project/issues)\n"
"- Check the [FAQ](./faq.md) document\n"
"- Join our [Discord community](https://discord.gg/your-invite-link) for communication\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"Happy coding! 🚀\n"

msgid "快速入门"
msgstr "Quick Start"

msgid "项目介绍"
msgstr "Project Introduction"

msgid "**Triton-Ascend**是适配华为Ascend处理器的Triton优化版本，用于高效进行核函数自动调优、算子编译及部署，通过兼容Triton核心语法并针对昇腾NPU特性进行深度优化，能够帮助用户在昇腾平台上快速开发和部署高性能计算任务。"
msgstr "**Triton-Ascend** is an optimized version of Triton adapted for Huawei Ascend processors, used for efficient kernel auto-tuning, operator compilation, and deployment. By being compatible with Triton core syntax and performing deep optimization for Ascend NPU features, it helps users quickly develop and deploy high-performance computing tasks on the Ascend platform."

msgid "本文以**Ubuntu 22.04**环境下通过软件包部署方式在线安装并运行向量加法实例为例，指导用户快速上手使用**Triton-Ascend**。如需体验更多安装方式请阅读[安装指南](./installation_guide.md)文档。"
msgstr "This document uses the deployment of a vector addition example via software package installation in an **Ubuntu 22.04** environment as an example to guide users in quickly getting started with **Triton-Ascend**. For more installation methods, please refer to the [Installation Guide](./installation_guide.md) document."

